xamine the specific amounts for the regular weekly and tax anticipation Treasury bills on January 31, 1970. The table reveals the total amount outstanding for each category, showing the breakdown of Treasury bills for that specific date.\n\nI notice the monthly issues for regular bills range from January to December 1970, with varying amounts from $1,501 to $16,525. The tax anticipation bills include March, April, and June 1970, totaling $9,274 million. These figures represent the specific issue months, providing a clear picture of the Treasury bill landscape for January 31, 1970.\n\nFor the 1975 data, I'll need to calculate the total regular weekly and annual maturing bills from February 1975 through January 1976, noting the additional entries beyond January 31, 1975.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_c4026e9118b5e293","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport math\n\n# 1970 data (from treasury_bulletin_1970_03_page_88.txt)\n# For January 31, 1970, we need the bills outstanding on that date\n# Regular weekly and annual maturing - sum of all entries listed:\n# Jan 1970 to Dec 1970\nregular_1970 = 1501 + 13510 + 13516 + 16525 + 6308 + 6512 + 7721 + 1701 + 1505 + 1003 + 1001 + 1002\n\n# Tax anticipation Treasury bills\ntax_1970 = 1752 + 3014 + 4508\n\n# For 1975 data, for January 31, 1975, we need bills outstanding on that date\n# Looking at the table - regular weekly and annual maturing from Feb 1975 to Jan 1976\n# But for January 31, 1975, we include bills that would be outstanding at that date\n# The table shows Feb 1975 through Jan 1976 (12 months)\nregular_1975 = 20916 + 20031 + 20328 + 14812 + 13517 + 14819 + 1803 + 1803 + 2003 + 2002 + 2001 + 2001\n\n# Tax anticipation - for 1975: April and June 1975\n# Note: These would be the tax anticipation bills outstanding at Jan 31, 1975\ntax_1975 = 2251 + 1256\n\n# Absolute changes\nregular_change = abs(regular_1975 - regular_1970)\ntax_change = abs(tax_1975 - tax_1970)\n\n# Euclidean norm\neuclidean_norm = math.sqrt(regular_change**2 + tax_change**2)\n\nprint(f\"1970 Regular weekly and annual maturing: {regular_1970}\")\nprint(f\"1970 Tax anticipation: {tax_1970}\")\nprint(f\"1975 Regular weekly and annual maturing: {regular_1975}\")\nprint(f\"1975 Tax anticipation: {tax_1975}\")\nprint(f\"Absolute change regular: {regular_change}\")\nprint(f\"Absolute change tax: {tax_change}\")\nprint(f\"Euclidean norm: {euclidean_norm}\")\nprint(f\"Euclidean norm rounded to nearest hundredth: {round(euclidean_norm, 2)}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
